     "title": "General cargo ships 400-5,000 GT and offshore ships under EU MRV since 2025; report examining their EU ETS inclusion due 31 December 2026",
     "sourced_finding_md": "- FuelEU Maritime applies to vessels above 5,000 gross tonnage calling at European ports with a 2% reduction that the source calls 'this year' (the step applies from 2025 and is in force) and 80% by 2050 [section_claim_provenance:807b3e3b-48cc-44b2-9327-99b48078a430]; the reductions are an annual average carbon intensity reduction compared to the average in 2020, starting with a 2% decrease by 2025 [section_claim_provenance:85d9a76e-5ac8-4cca-83af-4ee982d3940f].\n- The IMO Net-Zero Framework applies to oceangoing ships over 5,000 GT, ships under 5,000 GT are not covered, and discussions are underway on ships between 400 and 5,000 GT; the MEPC met on 14-17 October and agreed to adjourn for one year until 2026; the cluster holds no record of whether the adjourned session has since met or of its outcome [section_claim_provenance:d5c5f703-b8d1-4711-9d86-df4722fc37da].\n- A market-surface row quotes an April 2025 IMO statement that adoption was set for October 2025 before entry into force in 2027 [section_claim_provenance:b7c96db7-0ed9-456e-90af-844a0fce9175]; that adoption date did not hold, per the adjournment recorded in [section_claim_provenance:d5c5f703-b8d1-4711-9d86-df4722fc37da].\n- From 1 January 2025 general cargo ships between 400 and 5000 GT and offshore ships of 400 GT and above fell under the amended MRV Regulation [section_claim_provenance:476a1d5f-454d-4a29-84d8-118ee9340ef8].\n- Directive 2003/87 requires a Commission report by 31 December 2026 on including emissions from ships below 5 000 GT but not below 400 GT, and a Commission report on applying the system to more than 50% of extra-EU voyage emissions if the IMO does not adopt a comparable global measure by 2028 [item_forward_events:061f527f-8a70-41e2-987f-ffd63b6f93e1].\n- On the market surface, the EU ETS has covered CO2 emissions from all large ships of 5 000 gross tonnage and above entering EU ports since January 2024 [section_claim_provenance:8ffe3e3a-07ed-4283-a111-69e1c2e11745].",
