      },
      {
       "text": "*Analytical inference (cross-surface direction):* the market-surface rows state that the EU ETS (since January 2024) [section_claim_provenance:8ffe3e3a-07ed-4283-a111-69e1c2e11745], FuelEU Maritime [section_claim_provenance:807b3e3b-48cc-44b2-9327-99b48078a430] and the IMO framework [section_claim_provenance:b7c96db7-0ed9-456e-90af-844a0fce9175] cover ships of 5,000 gross tonnage and above; the regulations-surface rows state that general cargo ships between 400 and 5000 gross tonnage and offshore ships of 400 gross tonnage and above have been under MRV since 1 January 2025 [section_claim_provenance:476a1d5f-454d-4a29-84d8-118ee9340ef8] and that the Commission report examining the inclusion of ships below 5 000 but not below 400 gross tonnage in the EU ETS is due by 31 December 2026 [item_forward_events:061f527f-8a70-41e2-987f-ffd63b6f93e1]. Read together, operators of those smaller ships, monitored but outside the ETS coverage the market rows describe, face that report in the 0-6 month window; the rows state an examination, not a decision.",
